## 7. Swarm Task Breakdown

### Opus @ Medium — Orchestrator Track

**DB Schema + Migration** (runs first, unblocks everything else)
- File: `backend/src/models/notebookSchema.ts`
- Task: Full DDL, `runNotebookMigrations(db)`, `addColumnIfMissing`-style safety
- Parallel: Write `notebookService.ts` CRUD skeleton with all SQL prepared statements

**API Route Registration + Integration**
- File: `backend/src/routes/notebookRoutes.ts`
- Task: Wire all 18 routes; instantiate all services; pass `db` correctly; handle multipart via `multer` (add dep); all `authMiddleware` guards
- Also handles: the two-line modification to `backend/src/routes/api.ts` and the one-line addition to `backend/src/models/database.ts`

**Swarm State Tracking**
- Maintain a shared `NOTEBOOK_SWARM_STATE.md` or inline comment headers so the heavy-lifter Sonnet instance knows which service interfaces are locked and ready for implementation

### Sonnet @ Max — Heavy Lifter Track

**Group A — Backend Services** (can run in parallel after schema is locked)

1. `notebookIngestService.ts`
   - PDF text extraction: use `pdf-parse` (new dep)
   - DOCX: use `mammoth` (new dep)
   - URL: use `node-fetch` (already dynamically imported in api.ts) + JSDOM or `@mozilla/readability` (new dep) for main-content extraction
   - Chunking: fixed 512-token windows with 64-token overlap (estimate tokens by word count × 1.35)
   - Embedding: call `neuralForge.getEmbedding(chunk)` — the exact same method used by `VectorSearchService`
   - File storage: multipart uploads saved to `backend/data/notebook-uploads/` via `multer` disk storage

2. `notebookTranscribeService.ts`
   - Local path: POST to `http://localhost:11434/api/transcribe` (Ollama Whisper endpoint)
   - Fallback: OpenAI `whisper-1` via existing `openaiProvider.ts` — add a `transcribeAudio(filePath)` method
   - Detection logic: try local, if HTTP 404 or non-200 within 10s, fall to OpenAI

3. `notebookRagService.ts`
   - Retrieval: same cosine similarity approach as `VectorSearchService` — copy the algorithm, query against `notebook_chunks` only
   - Prompt assembly: context window limit 8000 tokens; top-5 chunks; inline citations as `[SOURCE: title, chunk N]`
   - SSE streaming: open Ollama `/api/chat` exactly like the existing `/api/oracle/stream` handler in `api.ts` — this is the proven pattern to replicate

4. `notebookDocGenService.ts`
   - Per `doc_type`, dispatch a specialized system prompt; stream tokens; accumulate; call `notebookService.saveDoc()` on completion

5. `notebookPdfExportService.ts`
   - Launch Puppeteer (add dep `puppeteer-core` + `@sparticuz/chromium` for local, or just `puppeteer` since this is desktop-local)
   - Template: branded minimal HTML matching the NUDIMMUD aesthetic (dark bg, JetBrains Mono, cyan-glow accents — same CSS variables as the frontend)
   - Output path: `backend/data/notebook-exports/<docId>.pdf`

6. `notebookObsidianSyncService.ts`
   - Use the existing `obsidianRest.client.patch('/vault/<path>', content)` pattern visible in `obsidianRestService.ts` line 633
   - Target folder: `NISABA/09_NOTEBOOK/` (new subfolder, consistent with existing NISABA structure)
   - Filename: `<doc_type>-<timestamp>-<sanitized_title>.md`

7. `notebookVizService.ts`
   - All four viz types: call `neuralForge.chat()` with structured extraction prompt requesting JSON output
   - Parse JSON from response; validate; return typed data
   - Cache results in-memory with 5-minute TTL (Map + timestamp) to avoid re-running LLM on every render

**Group B — React Components** (can start after API route surface is finalized)

All components live in `src/components/Oracle/NotebookTab/`.

1. `notebookBridge.ts` — frontend API client
   - `createNotebook()`, `listNotebooks()`, `deleteNotebook()` — all via `apiFetch`
   - `uploadSources(notebookId, files)` — `FormData` POST
